 The 500 customers live in `src/main/resources/customers.csv` and are loaded once
 at startup.

+## Filtering
+
+The list can be narrowed by name and by status. A customer has to satisfy both
+filters: every whitespace-separated term of the name search has to appear in the
+first or last name — ignoring case and accents, so `makinen` finds `Mäkinen` —
+and the status has to be one of the selected ones, all of them if none is.
+
+The filter is applied by the repository, before paging, so a filtered grid still
+fetches one page at a time and takes its row count from a count query. A line
+above the grid reports that count as `Showing 137 of 500`.
+
+The filter is also part of the URL, as the `name` and `status` query parameters
+(`/?name=vir&status=ACTIVE,CLOSED`), so a narrowed list can be bookmarked or
+sent to a colleague. Typing replaces the current history entry rather than
+pushing a new one.
+
 `CustomerRepository` deliberately behaves like a real paged backend: it refuses
 to return more than `MAX_PAGE_SIZE` (200) rows in a single call. Callers page.

